# G5 held past the tap window (sthold.h's STH_TAP_MS, 300 ms, and the engine's 20 ms margin): the whole mix stutters
# (engine/sthold.c). The first song is at 81 BPM (a 16th 185 ms, a beat 741 ms, a bar 2963 ms). Held for about 2 bars:
# "STUTTER" said once past the window, the catch on the first 16th line 320 ms or more after the press (hold_ms, under
# 320 ms and a 16th), an 8th repeated, then a step faster on each beat line (16th, 32nd, 64th, where it stays), G5 lit
# meanwhile; let go, live on the next 16th. A stutter on demand (G5
# tapped twice: a complex one, queued in the intro: tests/scenarios/stutter.vnl's song, its first landing bar 16, from 0: 15) that a hold keeps
# from its catch waits for the next group's last bar (bar 24, from 0: 23). Stopped, G5 held does nothing.
listen
wait 1400
tap PLAY
wait 3900
expect playing 1
tapkey 26
tapkey 26
wait 1
said STUTTER COMPLEX
expect stutter 2
key 26 down
wait 280
said_none
expect hold -1
wait 270
said STUTTER
expect hold 0
expect hold_in >0
expect hold_in <3
expect hold_ms >319
expect hold_ms <506
expect key_lit >67108863
# the 8th's first step on the first beat line once it has repeated whole (4-7 16ths), then a beat each
wait 5730
expect hold 3
expect hold_1 >3
expect hold_1 <8
expect hold_2 4
expect hold_3 4
expect hold_offbeat 0
key 26 up
wait 250
expect hold -1
expect hold_out 0
# the complex one still waits: G5 blinks quickly again (the held stutter's light off)
expect stutter_blink 125
said_none
# a short hold (about a beat): the catch, the 8th repeated, live again
wait 2000
key 26 down
wait 700
expect hold 0
key 26 up
wait 250
expect hold -1
expect hold_out 0
# held over the on-demand stutter's bar (bar 16, from 0: 15; 45.9-48.9 s): from its 4th 16th into the next bar
wait 31820
expect bar 15
expect stutter_fig >2
key 26 down
wait 2700
expect bar 16
expect hold >1
expect stutter 2
expect stutter_bar -1
key 26 up
wait 250
expect hold -1
# queued again: it lands on the next group's last bar (bar 24, from 0: 23; about 68.6-71.6 s)
wait 21500
expect bar 23
expect stutter_bar 23
expect stutter_fig >2
wait 300
expect stuttering 1
wait 2000
expect bar 24
expect stutter 0
# stopped: nothing
tap PLAY
wait 200
expect playing 0
said STOP
key 26 down
wait 400
expect hold -1
expect key_lit <67108864
said_none
key 26 up
wait 100
